From 23ac35b82a0f04700d6025d3abd4a64beb4e3956 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:44:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(renovate): hold Node below 26 until AWS Lambda nodejs26.x
 is GA

Netlify runs server functions on nodejs24.x while Lambda's nodejs26.x is a
public preview, so a Node 26 build with @types/node 26 typechecks APIs that
then throw in production. Renovate opened "update node.js to v26" PRs on eight
fleet repos and reddoor-md-pdf anyway. One allowedVersions "<26.0.0" rule on
depNames node and @types/node, scoped to no manager, covers every manager a
Renovate 44.199.2 dry run extracted Node from (nvm, nodenv, asdf, dockerfile,
npm engines, github-actions setup-node). Node 24 patches and minors still flow.
validate.yml asserts each leg stays capped.

Patch from reddoorla/reddoor-maintenance (P1-105; reddoor-workspace decisions
2026-11-04-1809-erp-node26-functions-stay-on-24 and
2026-11-09-1934-p1-105-msot-node26-merged-against-hold, answer (a)).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013FT5PBubSxSsJCqr6bizhQ
